          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Google confirms criminals used AI-built zero-day exploit in planned mass hacking campaign",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "Google's Threat Intelligence Group (GTIG) has confirmed that criminal actors used an AI-generated zero-day exploit as part of a planned large-scale hacking campaign, marking a significant escalation in AI-assisted cybercrime. The report indicates AI-powered attack capabilities have moved well beyond simple phishing emails and chatbot-assisted social engineering into the creation of novel software vulnerabilities. Security experts warn the finding signals a new threat threshold that existing defensive frameworks were not designed to address.",
            "url": "https://www.theregister.com/ai-ml/2026/05/11/google-says-criminals-used-ai-built-zero-day-in-planned-mass-hack-spree/5237982",
